{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>At that time.</b> In the forty days mentioned." "<b>An ark of wood.</b> The translators, of blessed memory, said that Moses first made a different ark, and the proof is \"and I made an ark\" [ואעש ארון], and afterward he said \"and I hewed\" [ואפסול], and he said \"and I placed the tablets in the ark that I made\" [ואשים את הלוחות בארון אשר עשיתי]. Their knowledge is broader than our knowledge, for it seemed to us that \"and the glory of YHWH dwelt\" [וישכון כבוד ה'] is joined with the glory that the elders saw, and we would not know when Moses went up, for it would appear by way of peshat that Moses fasted only eighty days, for the meaning of \"I stood on the mountain like the first days\" [אנכי עמדתי בהר כימים הראשונים] is a substitution, and the sense is: as when I stood on the mountain those forty days, YHWH heard me and said, \"Go, set out\" — and this is \"Go, lead the people\" — and so there would be an ark of wood by command, and it is the ark that Bezalel made."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {1 "המעתיקים resolved as 'the translators'; could alternatively mean 'the transmitters [of tradition].' The argument turns on tense/sequence of the cited verses in Deut. 10."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:22:58.371838360Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}